Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the ImageMagick module
=================================================

qore-imagemagick-module ships native ImageMagick 7 bindings, the
ImageMagickDataProvider source/AOT module, qimage and its manual, compiler
metadata and its matching architecture-independent common package contains
provider sources, resources and locale catalogs. The doc package contains
both API references and examples. Debhelper generates native/AOT debug symbols.

Use an isolated native environment with packaged Qore and libqore-dev, then
install debian/control's Build-Depends. Qualification targets Ubuntu 26.04
amd64 with Qore 3.0. Other targets need matching SDKs and native tests. Cross
builds fail explicitly because Qore tools run during compilation. ImageMagick
7 is required: releases shipping version 6 need a separately maintained v7
package. Use distribution libraries and their delegate/security configuration;
no private library, bundled source or build-time download is used. DejaVu and
URW fonts provide text rendering without a desktop. Supported image formats
and operations remain subject to ImageMagick's installed delegates and policy.

The minimum Qore runtime and libqore SONAME versions come from the installed
SDK; dh_shlibdeps supplies other library versions. The runtime package is not
Multi-Arch: same. AOT is enabled, source-tree qmod symlinks are disabled, and
noopt selects optimization level zero. QCC_JOBS=1 fixes partitioning across
CPU counts/jobserver loads while independent targets compile in parallel.
Qore tools use this build and the packaged standard library only. Prefix maps
cover native/AOT output; timezone and locale are fixed.

The stripping wrapper copied from Qore preserves appended AOT metadata; its
real-ELF tests run during builds. dwz excludes unsupported LLVM DWARF. All
provider catalogs and the ownership manifest are packaged; complete standard
locales are checked against the built provider with qore-misc-tools.

Source preparation and qualification
------------------------------------

Use a fresh version for each changed upload. This snapshot precedes 1.0.0.
From a clean committed checkout:

    version=1.0.0~git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../imagemagick-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-imagemagick-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../imagemagick-package-work/qore-imagemagick-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../imagemagick-package-work/qore-imagemagick-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../imagemagick-package-work
    cp -a debian "../imagemagick-package-work/qore-imagemagick-module-$version/"
    cd "../imagemagick-package-work/qore-imagemagick-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc into a fresh directory and run dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc
unprivileged offline. -B builds runtime/debug only; -A builds shared data and
documentation. The runtime depends on the common package at its exact source
version, allowing architecture-only binary rebuilds without rebuilding shared data.
nodoc in DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS suppresses HTML, and the nodoc profile also omits
the doc package. Full qualification runs tests; repeated/profile builds may
use nocheck. Retain and review any upstream test skips for missing delegates
or deliberately invalid fixture data instead of disabling distribution policy.

Run both upstream suites, complete catalogs, AOT helper tests and CLI checks.
Installed tests copy only test scripts into a temporary directory and preload
the installed AOT provider. CLI tests cover resize, PNG/JPEG conversion, text,
spaced paths and explicit in-place editing. A fresh qcc executable checks named
arguments, a PNG round trip and provider discovery. No external service is needed.

Check Lintian, hardening/debug symbols, AOT trailers, source/resource/catalog
parity, runtime-only installation without SDK, docs/debug coinstallation,
dpkg -V, purge/reinstall and byte reproducibility across paths/job counts.
Retain hashes, dependency inventories and logs. Testing-PPA publication is
separate from approval for a final general release.
